## Runtime dependencies

The two direct production dependencies are:

| Package | Version constraint | License |
|---|---|---|
| [`@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk) | `^1.12.1` | MIT (Anthropic, PBC) |
| [`ws`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/ws) | `^8.18.0` | MIT (Einar Otto Stangvik) |

The full transitive production dependency tree (93 packages as of v1.1.0)
consists of MIT, ISC, BSD-2-Clause, and BSD-3-Clause licensed code. None
require source-availability or copyleft propagation. All require attribution
preservation in distributions of derivative works.

When sr-truenas-mcp is installed via `npm install`, the package manager
fetches each dependency separately and the dependency's own `LICENSE` file
ships with its source — attribution is preserved automatically.

When sr-truenas-mcp is distributed as the **standalone Linux binary**
(`dist/sr-truenas-mcp` from `npm run build:binary`), the binary statically
embeds bundled dependency code via esbuild + pkg, so the attribution must be
shipped alongside the binary. The binary's source-of-truth dependency tree
can be reproduced with `npm ls --omit=dev --all`; each dependency's license
text is preserved in its respective `node_modules/<pkg>/LICENSE` file at
build time.
